aarch64 #23 milestone-1: port-returning kernel queries served in-guest (host_get_clock_service 206,
task special ports 3409/3418).

Extends the in-guest kernel-query synthesis (0051) to the PORT-returning queries. Adds a tiny guest
port table: inguest_mint_port() hands out names in a reserved high range (0xE0000000+) that ciderd
never assigns. mach_msg_overwrite_trap_impl synthesizes the COMPLEX reply (Head COMPLEX + msgh_body
{count=1} + one MOVE_SEND port descriptor, 40 bytes, matching ciderd's bytes) for
host_get_clock_service (206 -> minted clock port) and the two task special-port queries (3409 ->
MACH_PORT_NULL, as ciderd returns; 3418 -> minted port). deallocate/mod_refs on a minted name are
served in-guest (the guest owns it; RPCing an unknown name would error and abort the trap).

exec-true only FETCHES these ports (never sends to them), so a minted name that is stored and freed
at exit suffices. Verified with 0051: exec-true drops all 4 self-contained kernel queries
(200/206/3409/3418) to 0 ciderd RPC -- RECV 70 -> 58 (-12 RPCs/spawn), rc=0, soak 10/10. Flag-off
unchanged. On top of 0051.

